    "review": {
      "scope": "reviewed_computational_example",
      "interpretation": "Three connected 30-heavy-atom scaffold hypotheses were generated in three native attempts; none retains the starting scaffold. Candidate 3 was prepared in its unchanged chemical state with ten converged MMFF94s conformers; the lowest reported energy selects record 3 (zero-based record 2). Matched GNINA searches retain twenty poses each for the paired predicted STAT6 436-658 receptor and the independently prepared 9BIG experimental construct, using the same ligand, reference, seed and search budget. Both nearly tied leading predicted-domain poses and the leading experimental-receptor pose have 15 assessed native quality passes, six unassessed environmental checks and one not-applicable check. Native files and computed source frames remain unchanged; actual 2D/3D selection and original SDF downloads were reviewed.",
      "limitations": "This bounded computational tutorial is not a validated hit-finding campaign, binding-mode determination or affinity/selectivity measurement. Three generated molecules are not an enrichment benchmark or evidence of drug activity. The two best predicted poses differ by 4.61 A despite a score gap of 0.00661 kcal/mol; the experimental top pose differs by 11.20 A from the predicted top and is closest to predicted rank 14 (1.74 A). Receptor conditions change rankings. AK-1690 has a different graph and defines search extent only; no generated-ligand reference RMSD is inferred. The predicted reference placement has severe clashes, and the experimental construct has unresolved regions. Water/cofactor context is absent; six native true flags are unassessed. Quality plausibility and native UFF diagnostics do not prove binding or reduced MMFF strain. No dynamics or FEP was performed.",
      "checked": [
        "input_identity",
        "method_scope",
        "native_outputs",
        "visual_preview",
        "downloads"
      ]
    },
